<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-21165] .NET platform test timeouts after ClientServerCompatibilityTest</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-21165</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;There are many timeouted test runs in the .NET suite. Example:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci2.ignite.apache.org/buildConfiguration/IgniteTests24Java8_PlatformNetCoreLinux/7678070&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci2.ignite.apache.org/buildConfiguration/IgniteTests24Java8_PlatformNetCoreLinux/7678070&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
The build Ignite Tests 2.x (JDK 8/11)::Platform .NET (Core Linux) #39429 {buildId=7678070} has been running &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; more than 40 minutes. Terminating...
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Looks like only port 47500 is requested while server node started on another. Probably a previous test didn&apos;t release the port yet.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
Successfully bound communication NIO server to TCP port [port=47101, locHost=/127.0.0.1, selectorsCnt=4, selectorSpins=0, pairedConn=&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
Failed to connect to any address from IP finder (make sure IP finder addresses are correct and firewalls are disabled on all host machines): [/127.0.0.1:47500]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It looks like this issue happens on JDK8 only. And only on Linux. &lt;em&gt;ClientServerCompatibilityTest&lt;/em&gt; starts a server node with &lt;em&gt;Runner.java&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;PlatformProcessUtils#startProcess()&lt;/em&gt; and stops with &lt;em&gt;PlatformProcessUtils#destriyProcess()&lt;/em&gt;. On Windows, additional &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
 serverProc.KillProcessTree();
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;is applied.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We should wait until &lt;em&gt;java.lang.Process&lt;/em&gt; completely stops. &lt;/p&gt;




</description>
